INTERPRETATION
Let H_(n,t)(z)=P_(n,t)(z)F(z), with the notation of Lemma 5A8H26.
The coefficients of H/(1-z) and H/(1-z)^2 are respectively the first
and second cumulative coefficients tested above.  Both proposed
coefficientwise sufficient conditions are false.  The exact division
G=FE also found no decrease in the first-passage coefficients of E,
consistent with the elementary initial-neighbour loop injection, but
that scalar monotonicity is insufficient.  The strengthened
milestone-loop factor removes

  L=2+floor((K-2Q)/(Q+1))

independent geometric-series factors from E.  Its exact residual had
no negative coefficient in the displayed audit.  This is an audit of
Lemma 5A8H28T; the path-bijection proof is unbounded.

